[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one parser bug, one fix queued. The reports merged
into it show three problems. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: the parser is fixed, and the
booking-v3 form is retired. That closes two of the three.

<Callout kind="warn">
The one-day moves are still open. Neither the parser fix nor the retired form touches them.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

| problem | what the reports show | ticket | state |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | Day and month swapped: 7 April arrives as 4 July. Every tenant on file writes the day first, and the shared parser read every date month first. | [issue 1](https://github.com/mikebronner/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) | fixed 5 October: parse dd/mm for eu locales |
| `hint` | Day and month swapped, only through the booking-v3 form. The form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under a field it reads day first. The parser fix does not reach it. | [issue 2](https://github.com/mikebronner/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) | won't fix: booking-v3 form retired |
| one-day move | The date moves by one day, or two attendees see two different days. No swap. The desk files these under `parser` by tenant, in the note under the table above. | [issue 3](https://github.com/mikebronner/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3) | open: no fix yet |

The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. The tenant decides the cause, so the
"tagged as" column does not match the cause.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- Read what the reports show before you merge them. A swap and a one-day move are two bugs.
- One fix per ticket. If a fix cannot close every report in a ticket, split the ticket.

